  {
    "sha": "179b4423a7fd5a2d13041fd4c36b5eca2e39d2aa",
    "node_id": "C_kwDODp_HwtoAKDE3OWI0NDIzYTdmZDVhMmQxMzA0MWZkNGMzNmI1ZWNhMmUzOWQyYWE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Ryan Houdek",
        "email": "Sonicadvance1@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-09-05T03:01:34Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Ryan Houdek",
        "email": "Sonicadvance1@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-09-05T03:08:18Z"
      },
      "message": "Wine: Change behaviour around SMC and NtReadFile\n\nJIT invalidation around syscalls and kernel calls is mighty fickle.\nThis is why the previous code path was born. In order to properly handle\nthis case we need strong coordination between Wine and FEX around\ninvalidating code and memory protections. This doesn't quite exist today\nso we're kind of stuck with a kludge solution. Instead of forcing the\nPersona 5 code invalidation on to every process, only do it on P5R.\n\nThis fixes a hang in msiexec with PhysX trying to do a blocking read and\njitting code or creating threads, while also maintaining the P5R\napproach. The full comment is in the file about the reasoning.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "46eb9f0db087e271214fbe831bc9e34671e3b33e",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/FEX-Emu/FEX/git/trees/46eb9f0db087e271214fbe831bc9e34671e3b33e"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/FEX-Emu/FEX/git/commits/179b4423a7fd5a2d13041fd4c36b5eca2e39d2aa",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAARcAAAAHc3NoLXJzYQAAAAMBAAEAAAEBAKRVBEsHKfX4JA8aX7A6D0\ndx5Fx5cuItDKoR03jPEkLJZAgiqXj3+Sc9WhG60xGlXMSXbp3q2uMfxvr/+t0sw7QqmUMf\nnEU893GtLjAx4wXxx743p1vu/qaJ4H2Xbh9XwvVqyXd/2Sb4CNOQ33km83rxfvikqKNIBX\nrSGLb9Kyz99uJ2aREykzP+yGN+AQpINKhJH5iiBh7tviPUVtGjSHv3dv0C9Nd9InkwHxAp\nXoTHbY3qlD8V0e0Z1IKUBHCz/mTK52Duo6awCM9zWKwAYQuQXAXJsFIqXhBassGeT7CP+4\nHf9mPdTyIioVmOIVvGMQGiSYW13ZNLLCsInh0fEVkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIA\nAAEUAAAADHJzYS1zaGEyLTUxMgAAAQBlUoVmVDn9BaS7WLe2MDONTgk0WwShZI6RdhSZ43\ntrEdjHeqJIMW4zEDORyqjg7+vJcCBwYnQGo+7yzXb+8EMWTPLRfcLXzhoc/kA52kgQCPEm\n6HqUrDOJDa+bvoBc8eUZq8lkQ+qX+W/l9CUCh6989w/knrLhL8ebZPFqe7dKG228U9oiHJ\nyO3YyncbgRcTwP67/9uF25mQOWeRlvbn6loSL/asML8dw5q8gkmGb+eH1CBgumZm5Og0QB\nTKo81r+U8RY9BY/igNSOVtd76P4yuSRH+BH+dRWJBzHLwiKBvcS+dMul9Id9pO0irT8e4F\nYTyWIg6w4JxPxHolv0TSXq\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree 46eb9f0db087e271214fbe831bc9e34671e3b33e\nparent e3c6b37f706be93ffaa5f69ed1dba1964a131cc6\nauthor Ryan Houdek <Sonicadvance1@gmail.com> 1788577294 -0700\ncommitter Ryan Houdek <Sonicadvance1@gmail.com> 1788577698 -0700\n\nWine: Change behaviour around SMC and NtReadFile\n\nJIT invalidation around syscalls and kernel calls is mighty fickle.\nThis is why the previous code path was born. In order to properly handle\nthis case we need strong coordination between Wine and FEX around\ninvalidating code and memory protections. This doesn't quite exist today\nso we're kind of stuck with a kludge solution. Instead of forcing the\nPersona 5 code invalidation on to every process, only do it on P5R.\n\nThis fixes a hang in msiexec with PhysX trying to do a blocking read and\njitting code or creating threads, while also maintaining the P5R\napproach. The full comment is in the file about the reasoning.\n",
        "verified_at": "2026-09-05T03:08:27Z"
      }
    },
